\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Convention}
\title{Fixed-budget trace-selection protocol}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{harness}

\p{The trace intervention is a finite evaluation proposal. It compares
horizon and selector effects at a fixed retained budget while keeping the
model, teacher, scaffold, task split, verifier, seed law, and total token and
compute budgets visible. The source's selective-refinement intervention
supplies the comparison pattern, but the following arm matrix is an FTIP
protocol rather than a source result
\citet{Sections 6-7; Tables 4-5, 10}{dang2026selecting}.}

\p{Fix finite horizon labels #{\mathcal H}, selector labels #{\mathcal L},
state masks #{\mathcal M:=\mathcal P(\{s,h,w\})} from
\ref{ftip-00P0}, budget labels #{\mathcal B}, and split labels #{\mathcal D}.
An experimental arm is a tuple}
##{
 a=(H,\ell,M,B,D,\mathcal R)\in
 \mathcal A\subseteq\mathcal H\times\mathcal L\times\mathcal M
 \times\mathcal B\times\mathcal D\times\mathcal R,
}
\p{where #{\mathcal A} is finite. Each arm declares one model, teacher,
scaffold, verifier, task law, and inference protocol; those are held fixed
across its paired reset and continue runs. The arm's split #{D} declares
pairwise-disjoint selection and held-out task sets #{Q_{\rm sel}(D)} and
#{Q_{\rm hold}(D)} with #{|Q_{\rm hold}(D)|>0}, plus any cross-benchmark
split. The randomization law
#{\mathcal R} supplies paired seeds and the declared coupling.}

\p{Cross horizon and selection with the state masks in
\ref{ftip-00P0}. Each mask clears a selected subset of session context,
candidate history, and workspace coordinates; the lifecycle transition retains
the verified best candidate and its artifact. At minimum compare:}
\ol{
  \li{one-stage full-long traces;}
  \li{verification-preserving intermediate truncation;}
  \li{warm-start plus top-likelihood selection;}
  \li{warm-start plus bottom-likelihood selection;}
  \li{warm-start plus random selection at the same retained budget; and}
  \li{a coverage-stratified or diversity-preserving selector.}
}

\p{For arm #{a} and a positive run count #{N_a\in\mathbb N_{>0}}, with run
index #{i\in\{1,\ldots,N_a\}}, let #{\tau_{a,i}} be
termination, #{\tau^{\rm ev}_{a,i}} the declared evidence-or-recovery
boundary, and #{\tau^{\rm sat}_{a,i}} the first time the declared task-value
score reaches the arm's saturation threshold. Let #{G_{a,i}} mean that bounded
evidence gathering, verification, and any declared recovery event are present
in the retained trace; let #{F_{a,i}} mean that a verifier or execution failure
occurs before termination; and let #{V_{a,i}} mean that the final candidate passes
the declared verifier. Define the measurable indicators}
##{
 I^{\rm pre}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[\tau_{a,i}<\tau^{\rm ev}_{a,i}],\qquad
 I^{\rm prod}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[G_{a,i}],\qquad
 I^{\rm over}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[\tau_{a,i}>\tau^{\rm sat}_{a,i}],
}
##{
 I^{\rm rec}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[F_{a,i}\text{ and a declared recovery follows}],\qquad
 I^{\rm ver}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[V_{a,i}].
}
\p{The corresponding run rates use the declared denominator #{N_a}:}
##{
 (\widehat p^{\rm pre}_a,\widehat p^{\rm prod}_a,\widehat p^{\rm over}_a,
 \widehat p^{\rm rec}_a,\widehat p^{\rm ver}_a)
 =\frac1{N_a}\sum_{i=1}^{N_a}
 (I^{\rm pre}_{a,i},I^{\rm prod}_{a,i},I^{\rm over}_{a,i},I^{\rm rec}_{a,i},I^{\rm ver}_{a,i}).
}
\p{For the finite held-out task set, task coverage is
#{\widehat C^{\rm task}_a:=|\{q\in Q_{\rm hold}(D):q\text{ has an admitted
run}\}|/|Q_{\rm hold}(D)|}; for a declared finite strategy label set
#{\mathcal S_a} with #{|\mathcal S_a|>0}, strategy coverage is
#{\widehat C^{\rm strat}_a:=|\{s\in\mathcal S_a:s\text{ appears in an admitted
held-out trace}\}|/|\mathcal S_a|}. These positive denominators are reported
with the arm receipt.}

\p{Let #{\mathcal F^{\rm sel}_{a,i}} be the sigma-field generated by the
selection-time prefix, teacher-forced selector score, declared trace metadata,
and the arm's training/selection split. The selector is measurable with
respect to #{\mathcal F^{\rm sel}_{a,i}}; held-out task outcomes, verifier
outcomes, and post-selection continuation events are excluded from that
sigma-field. Pair every selected trace with its unselected continuation under
the same arm law, and reserve #{Q_{\rm hold}(D)} and the cross-benchmark split
for evaluation only.}

\p{The protocol charges selection, storage, restart, discarded-trace, and
verification costs, and retains the task, selector, budget, split, seed, and
randomization receipts. No claim that selected traces improve FTIP behavior is
established until an immutable experiment record contains these fields and the
finite rates and coverage denominators above.}
